e circadian clock. We introduce principles and processes associated with circadian gating in a variety of organisms, including some associated mechanisms. We highlight socioeconomic opportunities presented by the investigation of circadian gating, using selected examples from circadian medicine and agricultural crop production to illustrate its importance.\n\nThis article is part of the Theo Murphy meeting issue ‘Circadian rhythms in infection and immunity’."}],[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Keywords"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"review, circadian biology, clock-dependent responses, *collaborative work*"}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"detail-actions","children":[["$","a",null,{"className":"button button-primary","href":"https://royalsocietypublishing.org/doi/10.1098/rstb.2023.0346","children":"Article"}],null,null]}]]}]]}],["$","footer",null,{"className":"footer","id":"contact","children":[["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/kimmeylab/logo/ucsc logo.png","alt":"UC Santa Cruz"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Kimmey Lab"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Department of Microbiology and Environmental Toxicology"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Biomedical Sciences, UC Santa Cruz"}]]}]]}]]}]
